description:
Hosted model facts are scattered across the code:
- context_registry.py has one HOSTED_WINDOW = 1_050_000 and one HOSTED_OUTPUT_TOKENS = 4000 for every hosted model;
- llm.py keeps prices in a PRICES dict and reasoning levels in HOSTED_REASONING_EFFORTS;
- the Model DTO defaults context_window to 1050000.
This contradicts the catalog-not-hardcoded rule. On 2026-10-10 the user asked to embed each model's native context window in the model catalog metadata and manage limits from it. After discussing cost and industry practice, they decided to keep the 64K working budget (HOSTED_WORKING_CONTEXT_TOKENS) unchanged for now. Industry practice bounds per-question context below the native window: OpenAI file search uses about 16K of retrieved context, and Claude Projects switches to retrieval near the window. This ticket is catalog-only, with no change in behaviour.
